  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 245 AM MDT MON SEP 21 2026\nA ridge will remain over the area on Thursday. Thursday will be\nthe hottest day in the 7-day period, with temperatures near 90\ndegrees in lower elevations and 80 degrees in higher elevations. \nA trough moves into the Pacific NW Friday/Saturday with cooler \ntemperatures and increased chances (15 to 25 percent) of \nprecipitation this weekend. Precipitation chances will be \nhighest in Northeastern Oregon and West-Central Idaho, with \ngenerally dry conditions as one approaches the Nevada border. \nTemperatures fall to near normal on Friday, and 5 to 10 degrees\nbelow normal on Saturday and Sunday. The temperature drop may\nshift fully to Friday or Saturday as synoptic models come into\nbetter agreement on the cold front passage, causing a sharper\ncool off on Friday or prolonged warmness on Friday respectively.\nCooler temperatures remain through the weekend into next Monday\nas a trough axis entrenches itself along the coast and the jet\nstream stays overhead.",
